.\" Manpage for render (scenic-motion-engine offline renderer)
.TH RENDER 1 "2026-11-02" "scenic-motion-engine" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
render \- offline MP4 export CLI for scenic-motion-engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B render
[\fB\-\-audio\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-analysis\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\fB\-\-out\fR \fIPATH\fR
[\fB\-\-start\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-fps\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-width\fR \fIPX\fR]
[\fB\-\-height\fR \fIPX\fR]
[\fB\-\-fonts\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B render
drives the scenic-motion-engine offline renderer, producing an MP4 file by
evaluating a motion graph against an event source and muxing the result with
an optional audio track.
.PP
If
.B \-\-analysis
is omitted, a synthetic 120-BPM event source is substituted so a render can
be produced without a prior analysis pass. Only
.B \-\-out
is strictly required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-audio " " \fIPATH\fR
Input audio track (wav/mp3/flac/aac/m4a/ogg). Participates in the final mux
only; it does not drive motion events.
.TP
.BR \-\-analysis " " \fIPATH\fR
JSON analysis file produced by the analyzer binary. When omitted, a
synthetic 120-BPM source is used.
.TP
.BR \-\-out ", " \-o " " \fIPATH\fR
Output MP4 path. Required. Parent directories are created as needed.
.TP
.BR \-\-start " " \fISECONDS\fR
Start offset into the event source, in seconds. Default:
.BR 0 .
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fISECONDS\fR
Render length in seconds. Default:
.BR 10 .
.TP
.BR \-\-fps " " \fIN\fR
Frames per second. Default:
.BR 60 .
.TP
.BR \-\-width " " \fIPX\fR
Frame width in pixels. Default:
.BR 1920 .
.TP
.BR \-\-height " " \fIPX\fR
Frame height in pixels. Default:
.BR 1080 .
.TP
.BR \-\-fonts " " \fIDIR\fR
Directory to scan for fonts. Default:
.BR assets/fonts .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the built-in usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Render ten seconds with a precomputed analysis file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
render \\
    --audio    assets/audio/kafkaesque.wav \\
    --analysis analysis/kafkaesque.json \\
    --out      renders/out.mp4 \\
    --start 0 --duration 10 \\
    --fps 60 --width 1920 --height 1080
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quick preview from the synthetic 120-BPM source:
.PP
.RS
.nf
render --out renders/preview.mp4 --duration 4 --fps 30
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (missing input, I/O error, render error).
.TP
.B 2
Argument parse error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR analyze (1)
